{
  "_provenance": [
    "PRICE ARCHITECTURE — set in Phase 04 (docs/31-strategy-kpis.md), on the",
    "owner's instruction of 3 Sep 2026: an online agency working remotely across",
    "the Gulf and Egypt, pricing competitively as a new entrant.",
    "",
    "Currency is USD, not SAR. One remote agency serving several countries cannot",
    "quote a single national currency: SAR is meaningless to a buyer in Cairo or",
    "Dubai, and EGP moves too fast to publish. USD is what remote work in the",
    "region is quoted in.",
    "",
    "The figures sit at or just below the floor of the Egyptian market and clearly",
    "below the Gulf market (see docs/29-competitive-intelligence.md). That is the",
    "cheapest CREDIBLE band — the previous list sat below both markets entirely,",
    "in freelance-marketplace territory, which read as risk rather than as value.",
    "",
    "Previous list, for reversal (SAR): tier-starter 580, tier-professional 1180, tier-advanced 2580, web-landing 175, web-business 450, web-professional 700, soc-starter 150, soc-growth 250, soc-pro 450, ads-starter 150, ads-growth 225, ads-performance 400"
  ],
  "terms": {
    "_comment": [
      "SCOPE FACTS — wireframe W1, problem PS-05 (docs/30-problem-solution.md).",
      "The price is published; what it buys is not, and at the new band a buyer",
      "asks. Fill these in and the cards grow a facts block and a 'What's not",
      "included' disclosure. Leave a field empty and NOTHING renders for it — the",
      "page never shows a label with a blank beside it, and never guesses a value.",
      "",
      "`shared` applies to every package. Per-package `facts` (delivery, revisions)",
      "live on the package itself, beside its price.",
      "",
      "Write both languages. Plain words, no legal register: 'Two rounds of",
      "changes' beats 'client is entitled to two (2) revision cycles'."
    ],
